  "title": "இரவச்சம்",
  "heading": "2.31",
  "poet": "பல புலவர்கள்",
  "tinai": "unknown",
  "sangamTamil": "கரவாத திண்ணன்பின கண்ணன்னார் கண்ணும்\nஇரவாது வாழ்வதாம் வாழ்க்கை - இரவினை\nஉள்ளுங்கால் உள்ளம் உருகுமால் என்கொலோ\nகொள்ளுங்கால் கொள்வார் குறிப்பு.",
  "urai": null,
  "english": "Mendicancy is always painful. To live asking naught even from those dear as an eye, whose love is sure, and who never refuse, is happy life. Since the mind dissolves in shame at the very thought of beggary,— when men receive alms, what are the receivers' thoughts, I pray ?",
